==Old English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈseːon/|lang=ang}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*sehwaną}}, from {{der|ang|ine-pro|*sekʷ-|t=to see, notice}}. Cognate with {{cog|ofs|sīa}} ({{cog|fy|sjen}}), {{cog|osx|sehan}} ({{cog|nds|sehn}}), {{cog|odt|sian}} ({{cog|nl|zien}}), {{cog|goh|sehan}} ({{cog|de|sehen}}), {{cog|non|sjá}} (Danish and Swedish {{m|se|se}}, {{cog|is|sjá}}), {{cog|got|𐍃𐌰𐌹𐍈𐌰𐌽}}.

====Verb====
{{ang-verb|head=sēon}}

# to [[see]]

