===Etymology 2===
Akin to {{cog|osx|sīn|t=to be}}, {{cog|dum|sijn|t=to be}}, {{cog|goh|sīn|t=to be}}, {{cog|la|sum|t=(I) am}}. Ultimately from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{m|ine-pro|*h₁es-}}.

====Verb====
{{ang-verb|head=sēon}}

# To [[be]], used primarily in reference to God
#: '' Fæder ūser, þū sē '''eart''' on heofonum, '''sī''' þīn nama gehālgod '' &ndash; Our Father, who art in heaven, hallowed be thy name.

